  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A distillation tower, or crude oil distillation column, is a tall structure
    in refineries that separates crude oil into products like gasoline, diesel, and
    kerosene. The process begins by heating the oil so part of it vaporizes; lighter
    vapors rise while heavier liquids stay lower. Inside the column, trays and packing
    enhance separation, and at the top a condenser cools vapors into liquid collected
    in a reflux drum. Some liquid is withdrawn as product, while the rest is recycled
    to improve purity. With key parts like the reboiler, column body, condenser,
    and reflux drum, the tower efficiently purifies and fractionates crude oil into
    valuable fuels. \n\nPress the Button again in order to exit. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
